{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring Boot configuration properties to externalize and configure the logging directory (U2).",
    "Refactor the message-bus and serialization codec into a dedicated 'spring-bus' module, updating Maven dependencies in Spring XD to inherit these features (U3, U5).",
    "Refactor input/output type conversion logic into the 'spring-cloud-dataflow' repository to support custom domain objects (U4).",
    "Implement the 'singlenode' XD Admin SPI using an in-memory Module Launcher to allow local execution of data pipelines (U6).",
    "Implement the Diego Receptor XD Admin SPI by integrating with the Diego Receptor API to launch modules on CF Lattice/Diego (U7).",
    "Investigate the use of Spring Cloud Netflix Eureka or Consul for s-c-s modules to self-register to a service discovery mechanism (U8).",
    "Integrate the Hortonworks Connector for Teradata to resolve the NPE and enable Sqoop import jobs to Teradata (U1)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Access to the Spring XD, spring-bus, and spring-cloud-dataflow repositories is available with appropriate permissions.",
    "The Hortonworks Connector for Teradata is available and compatible with the current Sqoop version used in the project.",
    "The Diego Receptor API is accessible, documented, and a test environment is available for CF Lattice/Diego.",
    "The development environment is set up with Java 17+ and necessary build tools (Maven/Gradle).",
    "Unit and integration testing are included within the effort estimates for each activity."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Sqoop Teradata Integration",
      "activity_description": "Investigate the NPE when using the Teradata JDBC driver directly, and integrate the Hortonworks Connector for Teradata to allow Sqoop import jobs to connect to Teradata.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Configurable Logging Directory",
      "activity_description": "Refactor the hard-coded logging directory to be configurable via properties, allowing it to be set outside of xd.home (e.g., for RPM installations).",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Move message-bus to spring-bus",
      "activity_description": "Extract the message-bus code from the Spring XD repository into the spring-bus repository, update Maven dependencies, and ensure Spring XD inherits the features.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Move input/output type conversion to spring-cloud-dataflow",
      "activity_description": "Extract input/output type conversion logic from Spring XD to spring-cloud-dataflow to enable custom modules producing or consuming custom domain objects.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Move serialization codec to spring-bus",
      "activity_description": "Extract the serialization codec from the Spring XD repository into the spring-bus repository, update Maven dependencies, and ensure Spring XD inherits the functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Singlenode XD Admin SPI Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Develop a 'singlenode' (single JVM) implementation of the XD Admin SPI based on the Module Launcher to run data pipeline use-cases locally.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Diego Receptor XD Admin SPI Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement a Diego based Receptor implementation of the XD Admin SPI based on the ModuleLauncher to run data pipeline use-cases on CF Lattice/Diego.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Service Discovery Self-Registration Investigation",
      "activity_description": "Investigate the possibility of s-c-s modules self-registering themselves to a service discovery mechanism, allowing Spring XD runtime on CF to discover and orchestrate such modules through streams.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 41
  }
}
```

